  "summary": "The ancient Japanese art of paper marbling, where ink is floated on water and then transferred to paper to create delicate, swirling patterns.",
  "description": "Suminagashi produces ethereal, monochromatic patterns resembling smoke or water ripples, achieved by carefully controlling the flow of ink on the water's surface. The technique developed in Japan as a meditative practice and later influenced paper marbling traditions throughout Asia and Europe.",
